    <name>Johnny the Johnson</name>
    <metatype>Human</metatype>
    <background>Johnson is a Different Person each time, but always has the same personality, he’s at Personafix construct projected on a variety of rental bodies, each time, he’s uploaded into the Matrix by being inserted into a data jack. Johnson is a Different Person each time, but always has the same personality, he’s at Personafix construct projected on a variety of rental bodies, each time, he’s uploaded into the Matrix by being inserted into a data jack. “I remember the first time I was uploaded into the matrix, when the new sensors, the scanners pick up my presence the signal changes, the sound changes, all the red lights go off and then there’s a sudden crunch of air, like someone opened a gas chamber. The lights come on and a cool breeze washes over my skin as I remember myself. I was on a surface transport, this morning as I recall, I can’t exactly recall the details of what happened to me, but this morning the transport I was on was changed. It became part of the matrix and I was freed from all the people, to operate on my own and, “Johnson smiled. “But my heart was broken to hear the story you just told of what happened to Julia, not one word about how you can help me.” Johnson grinned, “At least, you were brave enough to tell me how much you care.” “You won’t help me Johnson, you’re a digital, you live within the matrix, I’ve already explained that.” Johnson nodded, “I’m a digital myself, I can speak to digital, digital bodies, so we have something in common. You say you can work with me, what would you want me to do, show you what to do, how to get to Gaia?” “No, Johnson,” she stopped him, “I can’t do</background>
